id: async-initial-values
title: Async Initial Values
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Forms often edit data loaded from an API. A server-state library should own\nfetching, caching, loading, and retries; TanStack Form should own the editable\ncopy."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are two supported approaches: wait to create the controller until the\ndata is ready, or create it immediately with complete fallback values. Choose\nthe one that matches the loading experience your element needs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"wait-before-creating-the-editor","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wait before creating the editor"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep the controller optional, fetch the data, and create it only after complete\ndefaults exist:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport {\n  TanStackFormController,\n  formOptions,\n  type LitFormType,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-form'\n\ntype User = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n}\n\nconst userFormShape = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n  },\n})\n\nclass UserEditor extends LitElement {\n  private form?: LitFormType<typeof userFormShape>\n  private loadError = false\n\n  connectedCallback() {\n    super.connectedCallback()\n    void this.loadUser()\n  }\n\n  private async loadUser() {\n    try {\n      const response = await fetch('/api/users/1')\n      const user = (await response.json()) as User\n\n      this.form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n        defaultValues: user,\n        onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n          await fetch('/api/users/1', {\n            method: 'PUT',\n            headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n            body: JSON.stringify(value),\n          })\n        },\n      })\n    } catch {\n      this.loadError = true\n    }\n    this.requestUpdate()\n  }\n\n  render() {\n    if (this.loadError) return html`<p role=\"alert\">Could not load.</p>`\n    if (!this.form) return html`<p>Loading…</p>`\n    return html`<form><!-- fields --></form>`\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is useful when no form state is needed during loading. Creating a fresh\neditor for a different record also makes record changes explicit."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"create-the-form-before-data-arrives","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create the form before data arrives"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provide a static, shape-complete fallback, then call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.update(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" when\nthe query result changes. Keep option creation in one function so callbacks and\nvalidation settings remain consistent."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { TanStackFormController, formOptions } from '@tanstack/lit-form'\n\nconst emptyUser: User = {\n  firstName: '',\n  lastName: '',\n}\n\nclass UserEditor extends LitElement {\n  private form = new TanStackFormController(this, this.options(emptyUser))\n\n  private options(defaultValues: User) {\n    return formOptions({\n      defaultValues,\n      onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n        await saveUser(value)\n      },\n    })\n  }\n\n  connectedCallback() {\n    super.connectedCallback()\n    void loadUser().then((user) => {\n      this.form.update(this.options(user))\n      this.requestUpdate()\n    })\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When loaded data replaces the fallback, TanStack Form applies the new defaults\nto untouched fields while preserving fields the user already touched. You can\nhide the fields during loading or render the empty form immediately."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The repository's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/lit/query-integration"},{"type":"text","value":" example demonstrates this\npattern with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryObserver"},{"type":"text","value":" from TanStack Query Core."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"background-refetches-and-record-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Background refetches and record changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" establish the baseline; they are not a fully controlled\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"values"},{"type":"text","value":" property. Later "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.update(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" calls preserve touched fields."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a background refetch arrives while a user is editing, decide whether to keep\nlocal edits, prompt before replacing them, or deliberately call\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.api.reset(nextValues)"},{"type":"text","value":". Do not overwrite in-progress input merely because\na query refreshed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When switching records, create a fresh editor element/controller or explicitly\nreset the existing form. Otherwise, touched values from the previous record can\nbe preserved when new defaults arrive."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"wait-before-creating-the-editor","text":"Wait before creating the editor","level":2},{"id":"create-the-form-before-data-arrives","text":"Create the form before data arrives","level":2},{"id":"background-refetches-and-record-changes","text":"Background refetches and record changes","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nForms often edit data loaded from an API. A server-state library should own\nfetching, caching, loading, and retries; TanStack Form should own the editable\ncopy.\n\nThere are two supported approaches: wait to create the controller until the\ndata is ready, or create it immediately with complete fallback values. Choose\nthe one that matches the loading experience your element needs.\n\n## Wait before creating the editor\n\nKeep the controller optional, fetch the data, and create it only after complete\ndefaults exist:\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport {\n  TanStackFormController,\n  formOptions,\n  type LitFormType,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-form'\n\ntype User = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n}\n\nconst userFormShape = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n  },\n})\n\nclass UserEditor extends LitElement {\n  private form?: LitFormType<typeof userFormShape>\n  private loadError = false\n\n  connectedCallback() {\n    super.connectedCallback()\n    void this.loadUser()\n  }\n\n  private async loadUser() {\n    try {\n      const response = await fetch('/api/users/1')\n      const user = (await response.json()) as User\n\n      this.form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n        defaultValues: user,\n        onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n          await fetch('/api/users/1', {\n            method: 'PUT',\n            headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n            body: JSON.stringify(value),\n          })\n        },\n      })\n    } catch {\n      this.loadError = true\n    }\n    this.requestUpdate()\n  }\n\n  render() {\n    if (this.loadError) return html`<p role=\"alert\">Could not load.</p>`\n    if (!this.form) return html`<p>Loading…</p>`\n    return html`<form><!-- fields --></form>`\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis is useful when no form state is needed during loading. Creating a fresh\neditor for a different record also makes record changes explicit.\n\n## Create the form before data arrives\n\nProvide a static, shape-complete fallback, then call `form.update(...)` when\nthe query result changes. Keep option creation in one function so callbacks and\nvalidation settings remain consistent.\n\n```ts\nimport { TanStackFormController, formOptions } from '@tanstack/lit-form'\n\nconst emptyUser: User = {\n  firstName: '',\n  lastName: '',\n}\n\nclass UserEditor extends LitElement {\n  private form = new TanStackFormController(this, this.options(emptyUser))\n\n  private options(defaultValues: User) {\n    return formOptions({\n      defaultValues,\n      onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n        await saveUser(value)\n      },\n    })\n  }\n\n  connectedCallback() {\n    super.connectedCallback()\n    void loadUser().then((user) => {\n      this.form.update(this.options(user))\n      this.requestUpdate()\n    })\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWhen loaded data replaces the fallback, TanStack Form applies the new defaults\nto untouched fields while preserving fields the user already touched. You can\nhide the fields during loading or render the empty form immediately.\n\nThe repository's `examples/lit/query-integration` example demonstrates this\npattern with `QueryObserver` from TanStack Query Core.\n\n## Background refetches and record changes\n\n`defaultValues` establish the baseline; they are not a fully controlled\n`values` property. Later `form.update(...)` calls preserve touched fields.\n\nIf a background refetch arrives while a user is editing, decide whether to keep\nlocal edits, prompt before replacing them, or deliberately call\n`form.api.reset(nextValues)`. Do not overwrite in-progress input merely because\na query refreshed.\n\nWhen switching records, create a fresh editor element/controller or explicitly\nreset the existing form. Otherwise, touched values from the previous record can\nbe preserved when new defaults arrive.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: async-initial-values\ntitle: Async Initial Values\n---\n\nForms often edit data loaded from an API. A server-state library should own\nfetching, caching, loading, and retries; TanStack Form should own the editable\ncopy.\n\nThere are two supported approaches: wait to create the controller until the\ndata is ready, or create it immediately with complete fallback values. Choose\nthe one that matches the loading experience your element needs.\n\n## Wait before creating the editor\n\nKeep the controller optional, fetch the data, and create it only after complete\ndefaults exist:\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport {\n  TanStackFormController,\n  formOptions,\n  type LitFormType,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-form'\n\ntype User = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n}\n\nconst userFormShape = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n  },\n})\n\nclass UserEditor extends LitElement {\n  private form?: LitFormType<typeof userFormShape>\n  private loadError = false\n\n  connectedCallback() {\n    super.connectedCallback()\n    void this.loadUser()\n  }\n\n  private async loadUser() {\n    try {\n      const response = await fetch('/api/users/1')\n      const user = (await response.json()) as User\n\n      this.form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n        defaultValues: user,\n        onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n          await fetch('/api/users/1', {\n            method: 'PUT',\n            headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n            body: JSON.stringify(value),\n          })\n        },\n      })\n    } catch {\n      this.loadError = true\n    }\n    this.requestUpdate()\n  }\n\n  render() {\n    if (this.loadError) return html`<p role=\"alert\">Could not load.</p>`\n    if (!this.form) return html`<p>Loading…</p>`\n    return html`<form><!-- fields --></form>`\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis is useful when no form state is needed during loading. Creating a fresh\neditor for a different record also makes record changes explicit.\n\n## Create the form before data arrives\n\nProvide a static, shape-complete fallback, then call `form.update(...)` when\nthe query result changes. Keep option creation in one function so callbacks and\nvalidation settings remain consistent.\n\n```ts\nimport { TanStackFormController, formOptions } from '@tanstack/lit-form'\n\nconst emptyUser: User = {\n  firstName: '',\n  lastName: '',\n}\n\nclass UserEditor extends LitElement {\n  private form = new TanStackFormController(this, this.options(emptyUser))\n\n  private options(defaultValues: User) {\n    return formOptions({\n      defaultValues,\n      onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n        await saveUser(value)\n      },\n    })\n  }\n\n  connectedCallback() {\n    super.connectedCallback()\n    void loadUser().then((user) => {\n      this.form.update(this.options(user))\n      this.requestUpdate()\n    })\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWhen loaded data replaces the fallback, TanStack Form applies the new defaults\nto untouched fields while preserving fields the user already touched. You can\nhide the fields during loading or render the empty form immediately.\n\nThe repository's `examples/lit/query-integration` example demonstrates this\npattern with `QueryObserver` from TanStack Query Core.\n\n## Background refetches and record changes\n\n`defaultValues` establish the baseline; they are not a fully controlled\n`values` property. Later `form.update(...)` calls preserve touched fields.\n\nIf a background refetch arrives while a user is editing, decide whether to keep\nlocal edits, prompt before replacing them, or deliberately call\n`form.api.reset(nextValues)`. Do not overwrite in-progress input merely because\na query refreshed.\n\nWhen switching records, create a fresh editor element/controller or explicitly\nreset the existing form. Otherwise, touched values from the previous record can\nbe preserved when new defaults arrive.\n"}
